      "problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)-4.$",
      "worked_solution": "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\nx>0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x),$ we replace $x$ with $\\frac{x}{2}-1$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}-1>0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-1 & >0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & >1 \\\\ x & >2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in (2,\\infty ).$",
